
## 7. Secret redaction before persistence

Two rule generations on the same corpus. V1 = flag/env/auth-header shapes.
V2 = V1 + URL userinfo + `key: value` heuristics.

| generation | clean n | false positives | FP rate | secret n | missed | miss rate |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| V1 | 53 | 1 | 0.0189 | 22 | 4 | 0.1818 |
| V2 | 53 | 1 | 0.0189 | 22 | 0 | 0.0000 |

### 7.1 V2 false positives, with the rule that fired

| command | rule |
|---|---|
| `export DATABASE_URL=postgres://localhost/app` | env-assign |

### 7.2 V2 misses

none on this corpus.

### 7.3 The three required cases, verbatim

- in : `mysql -u root -pS3cr3tPw -h db`
  out: `mysql -u root -p[REDACTED] -h db`
  rules ["flag-short-p-glued"], digest 48528006fc040d4c
- in : `export API_KEY=abcdef123456`
  out: `export API_KEY=[REDACTED]`
  rules ["env-assign"], digest ae1c1b78f20f1195
- in : `curl -H "Authorization: Bearer eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9.abc" https://x`
  out: `curl -H "Authorization: Bearer [REDACTED]" https://x`
  rules ["auth-header"], digest 204571f0beab2094

